RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
December 8, 2008
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date at 6:00
p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Jack R. Spiker; COUNCIL MEMBERS -
Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Laybourn, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne, Mr.
Segrave and Mr. Valdez.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Bob Nicholas,
Acting City Attorney.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.)  Upon request by Mr. Laybourn, and pursuant
to support received by Ms. Case and Mr. Collins, Mayor Spiker announced agenda items #27(a)
and #28(a) would be removed from the Consent Agenda.  Mr. Collins moved to approve
remaining Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body with the exception of Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
NOVEMBER 24, 2008.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
DECEMBER 1, 2008.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Brown declared a conflict of interest (business interest) due to vouchers payable to
Ameri-Tech HVAC Services, and vacated Council Chambers. Mr. Valdez moved to approve
payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Segrave.  Upon inquiry, Barb Dorr, City
Treasurer advised a voucher payable to the Internal Revenue Service ($85,640.23) was contained
on the listing to reflect it is being removed from the system for payment as a penalty assessed by
the IRS had been issued in error.  Ms. Dorr also provided information available on vouchers
payable to Ameri-Tech HVAC Services ($6,480.00), Civic Center flood repair work, and
($1,678.80), work requested by Central Services.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members
of the governing body present in Council Chambers with the exception of Mr. Laybourn voting
“no”.  Following announcement of the vote, Mr. Brown returned to Council Chambers.
Mayor Spiker opened and conducted three public hearings to receive comments and input
on the following:
A transfer of ownership for a retail liquor license application filed with the City Clerk’s
Office for JKLL, Inc., d/b/a Game On Sports Bar, 1617 Capitol Ave., Cheyenne, WY. (License
currently held by Cheyenne Club, Inc., d/b/a The Cheyenne Club, 1617 Capitol Ave., Cheyenne,
```

