Segrave moved to adopt with staff recommendations #1 through 3, seconded by Mr. Brown.
Discussion included the following topics: Concern with utilization of water and sewer services
from South Cheyenne Water and Sewer District vs. direct services from the Board of Public
Utilities (BOPU); District services received from BOPU; other options available; lack of City
oversight for services provided by the District, City standards and uniformity in requirements for
developers; City vs. County annexations affiliated with developments, and other developments
in the area.  Discussion followed and included input from R.C. Reiman, project developer, who
advised the development area is located within the serviceable boundaries of the South
Cheyenne Water and Sewer District.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the
governing body with the exception of Mr. Segrave voting “no”. (#5087)
