LEASES/CONTRACTS/LEGAL:
Contract between the City of Cheyenne and WINhealth Partners for city employee health
coverage. Jason Sanchez, President of the Cheyenne Public Employees Association, spoke in
support of the contract on behalf of the Association.  Mr. Segrave moved to approve, seconded
by Mr. Brown.  Discussion followed on health insurance cost increases for retirees;
WINHealth’s HMO (Health Maintenance Organization) plan structure, and health coverage plan
pricing and lack of  information, described as proprietary and confidential, received during the
bidding process.  Cheryl Hageman, HRH, consultant, advised it is not uncommon for some
insurance entities to not disclose pricing information between the company and health care
providers.  Upon inquiry, Rich Wiederspahn, Director of Human Resources, provided
information on communication efforts made to advise employees of the proposed insurance plan
and rates.  Discussion continued on premiums and deductible rates.  Beth Wasson, WINHealth
Partners, provided further information on non-disclosure of fees that are established between
health providers and WINHealth; HMO plan structure and local physician participation; patient
responsibilities involving co-payments, and usual and customary fee schedules under traditional
health care plans.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body with the
exception of Ms. Case and Mr. Laybourn voting “no”. (#5322)
[CA]
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, Transit Division, and Stride Learning Center,
to provide a bus for Stride clients to use for curb-to-curb public transportation -- referred to
Finance Committee.
[CA]
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and the Cheyenne/Laramie County
Corporation for Economic Development (LEADS) industrial and economic development
services -- referred to Finance Committee.
