### Page 7 of 8

```text
CONSIDERATION OF BIDS:
Consideration of Bid #M-7-09 for a contract between the City of Cheyenne, Engineering
Dept., and Tarco, Inc., Arvada, CO, for the Henderson Basin Flood Control Improvement Project
(2007-2010 1% Sales Tax).  John Fafoutakis expressed concern with the item being placed on
the Consent Agenda due to the amount of the bid.  Mr. Segrave moved to approve in an amount
not to exceed $2,888,909.58, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Upon inquiry, Ken Lewis, City Engineer,
provided project location information; advised overall future effect of the project will result in
reduction of the special flood hazard elevation in the Basin region, particularly during storm
events, and confirmed savings in the bid total of approximately $1 million.  During comments
involving the Consent Agenda process, Mr. Collins and Mr. Brown each raised points of order
that comments were not germane to the motion on the floor.  Mayor Spiker ruled that comments
could continue but should pertain to the motion. Following further comments on Consent
Agenda procedures, motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body. (#5323)
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-10-09 between the City of Cheyenne, Parks & Recreation, and
CPS Distributors, Inc., Cheyenne, WY for furnishing misc. irrigation supplies for the South
Cheyenne Community Park Project (1% Specific Purpose Sales & Use Tax).  Motion (per
Consent Agenda) carried (amount not to exceed $49,635.81).
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-13-09 between the City of Cheyenne, Street & Alley, and
Bobcat of Cheyenne, for furnishing one new rubber tire skid-steer loader and equipment with
trade-in of used loader (2007-2010 1% Sales Tax).  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried
(amount not to exceed $47,899.00).
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-14-09 between the City of Cheyenne, Sanitation Dept, and
Ameri-Tech Equipment Co., Evansville, WY, for furnishing a recycle depot (consisting of 6
individual 6-yard containers).  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried (amount not to exceed
$54,772.00).
[CA]
Consideration of Bid #R-12-09 between the City of Cheyenne, Sanitation Dept., and
American Scales, Inc. of Lakewood, CO, for furnishing and installing one new fully electronic
above ground steel deck truck scale with software -- referred to Finance Committee.
APPOINTMENTS:
Re-appointment of Mal Burnside, Al Cassidy, and Dan Edeen to the Contractor
Licensing Board.  Mr. Collins moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Comment followed
on placement of the item on the Consent Agenda and public recognition of individuals serving
on City boards.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.
ANNOUNCEMENTS/REPORTS/MOTIONS:
Announcement was made that due to the Christmas holiday, the next regular meeting of
the Governing Body will be held Monday, December 22, 2008 at 3:00 p.m. in City Council
Chambers.
