### Page 8 of 8

```text
Announcement was made that the Cheyenne City Council will hold a public hearing to
discuss the sale of the City-owned real property located at 700 West Fox Farm Road, Cheyenne,
Wyoming to Attention Homes, Inc. which sale will benefit the economic development of the
City of Cheyenne, pursuant to Wyo. Stat. § 15-1-112(b)(i)(D).  The estimated appraised value of
said property to be sold is $184,000 and will be sold to Attention Homes, Inc. for $2,000.  This
land will provide additional space to facilitate the expansion and redevelopment of Attention
Homes, Inc.  Under other City business, Mr. Pierson noted there was no date included in the
public hearing announcement.  City Clerk Carol Intlekofer stated her belief the hearing was
proposed to be held at the December 22 meeting (3:00 p.m.) and Mayor Spiker stated the
nd
matter would be reviewed with legal staff to determine whether re-advertising (i.e. rescheduling)
of the hearing date and time may be required for public notification.
Announcement was made of a public hearing to be held December 22, 2008 at 3:00 p.m.
in City Council Chambers for a restaurant liquor license application filed with the City Clerk’s
Office for Yu Zheng d/b/a Golden House Restaurant, 1651 Carey Ave., Ste. 8, Cheyenne, WY.
Announcement was made of the appointment of Tony Adams to the Personnel
Commission, Mark Hardee to the Fire Civil Service Commission, Michael Lemke to the
Housing and Community Development Advisory Council and Jody Malm and Beverly Bowman
to the Board of Adjustment, to be confirmed December 22, 2008.
OTHER CITY BUSINESS:
John Fafoutakis expressed his concerns with the volume of state-wide alcohol related
offenses and affiliated law enforcement time and expense.
City Councilwoman-elect Amber Ash commented on inaudible portions of City Council
meeting streaming video archives, due to persons not speaking directly into microphones, and
suggested a reminder be made at meetings to assist in improving the sound quality.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 7:51 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
December 19, 2008
